{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_016PzScrKF8ruAcQaypbfUpz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Anchor is a self-hosted personal productivity and R&D control system built for J.C. Liechty. Grounded claims about what it is and what it ships:\n\n**Purpose**\n- A single-folder (`C:\\dev\\Anchor`), plain-markdown task/project manager â€” no database, no syncing, no OneDrive â€” where markdown files are the source of truth and everything stays readable by any CLI or editor.\n- It manages a personal workflow: tasks with a full lifecycle (Active â†’ Done â†’ Cancelled â†’ Saved-for-Later â†’ Restored), projects across domains (academic, commercial, family, writing), a quick-capture inbox, and weekly reviews.\n\n**What it does / ships**\n- **`anchor_gui.py`** â€” the primary app: a stdlib-only Python HTTP server that renders an interactive browser dashboard at `http://localhost:8777` and writes directly back to the markdown files. It runs persistently as the NSSM Windows service `anchor` (not launched by hand).\n- **`anchor.py`** â€” a CLI engine mirroring the same logic (done/add/capture/cancel/save/restore), and it generates the static `dashboard.html`.\n- **`anchor_healthcheck.py`** â€” a daily 5 AM self-test (via Task Scheduler) that parses every file, exercises every endpoint on a throwaway port, walks a synthetic task through all states, and writes a dated report; failures surface as a red dashboard banner.\n\n**The larger half â€” an R&D \"trio\" control surface**\n- Beyond task tracking, Anchor has grown into mission-control for AI-assisted R&D driven by the skill trio **researchPrime (research) â†’ Crucible (planning) â†’ Foreman (build)**.\n- It has been built and merged through four design generations: **v2** (session model, cached/validated summaries, Grass Catchers idea lane, deliverable pinning, interactive REPL terminal), **v3 \"Mission Control\"** (real ConPTY terminals via the one declared native dependency `pywinpty`, per-session git-worktree isolation, a stacking window manager, in-place summaries, stage handoffs, runnable deliverable previews, Ghost World Labs branding), and **v4 \"Project Cockpit\"** (the current state: lane tiles with status lights, inline expanding panels with summary-over-terminal, a claudeâ†”gemini engine toggle, per-lane doc roles, project cost/tokens/time rollups, grass-idea promotion, and type-aware deliverable launch).\n- Each project gets a rich window (`GET /project/<id>`) where you launch the trio as durable, isolated, server-side terminal sessions that feel like a normal Claude Code / Gemini session â€” the lane's skill auto-loads once and greets once.\n\n**Constraints it holds itself to**\n- Python stdlib only, with exactly one declared exception (`pywinpty`, lazy, terminal-only, an optional `pip install .[terminal]` extra); `distro.py`'s import scan enforces \"no other native/third-party imports.\"\n- No binary/compiled assets; everything must stay accessible from any tool.\n\nOne caveat: this is grounded entirely in the project's own docs (CLAUDE.md and the locked North-Star/decision excerpts), which describe v4 as built, merged, and deployed â€” I didn't independently re-verify the running service or test counts for this summary."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45306,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6622d7d6-50d9-4642-848a-24b1ff240321","uuid":"67b5c09d-d347-4b75-979d-0e720983c36b","request_id":"req_011Cc1iAjoDMw5CvEkw2qAkP"}
